# Tests must not touch machine state (R1)

The AIC PIM workspace ships **long-running services**, **elevated
configurators**, **operator GUIs**, and **headless installers** that
all read from the same machine-global stores: `%PROGRAMDATA%\AIC\…` /
`/etc/aic/…`, Windows `HKLM`, Windows Credential Manager / macOS
Keychain / Linux Secret Service, named pipes under `\\.\pipe\…`,
process environment variables. A test that mutates any of those
stores is a **test-isolation bug**, not a "quirky test": parallel
tests in the same process see each other's mutations, the developer's
real installation gets corrupted, and the test passes on Tuesday and
fails on Wednesday because a sibling test ran first.

This rule binds the agent's test-authoring behavior AND the
production code shape that makes test-fixturing possible.

## The rule

> **Tests must drive the system under test through explicit
> per-test paths, handles, and channels — never through
> `std::env::set_var`, never through writes to shared machine
> stores. Production code that reads from machine-global state
> must expose a fixture API (`fn save_to_file_at(&Path)`,
> `fn open_at(channel: &str)`, `fn load_from_dir(&Path)`) so
> tests can bind their own sandbox without mutating the
> process.**

Concretely:

1. **No `std::env::set_var(` in test bodies.** `#[test]`,
 `#[tokio::test]`, `#[test_log::test]`, `rstest::*`, `criterion`
 benchmarks, `proptest!` blocks. The process environment is a
 single global; concurrent tests racing on it is undefined
 behavior in Rust 1.74+ (`set_var` is `unsafe` for exactly this
 reason).
2. **Production code that today reads an env var to locate a
 directory / pipe / file MUST also expose an explicit-path
 variant** that takes the resolved path / handle as an argument.
 Tests bind their own `tempfile::TempDir` and call the explicit
 variant; the env-var path remains as the production fallback
 (operator-controlled debug knob), but the test path does not
 traverse it.
3. **No test may write to a shared machine store** unless it lives
 under a per-test sandbox the test created and deletes on drop:
 - `%PROGRAMDATA%\AIC\…` / `/etc/aic/…` → write under a
 `tempfile::TempDir`; pass the path explicitly via the fixture
 API.
 - Windows `HKLM` / `HKCU` → use the `pim-config-storage`
 in-memory test backend (gated by `cfg(test)`), or a
 throwaway `HKCU\Software\AIC\test-<uuid>` subtree the test
 deletes in its `Drop`.
 - OS keyring → use the `pim-config-storage` in-memory backend
 with a **throwaway program id** (`pim-e2e-<uuid>`); never
 the production program id (`pim-offline-agent`,
 `pim-offline-server`, …).
 - Named pipes / Unix sockets → bind a per-test pipe name with
 a UUID suffix (e.g.
 `\\.\pipe\aic-test-{uuid}-elevation`) and pass it to the
 server / client constructors explicitly.

## Production env vars currently read in this workspace

The corrective contract requires that **every** entry in this table
either (a) keeps its env-var read for the production debug-knob
path AND grows an explicit-path sibling that tests use, or (b) loses
the env-var read entirely when the new fixture API lands. Today's
inventory (run `rg "env::var(_os)?\(\s*\"(OFFLINE_|AIC_|PIM_|LOCAL_UPDATE_|ENABLE_LEGACY_|OFFLINE_DEV_|OFFLINE_ADMIN_)" --type rust` to refresh):

| Env var | Read by (file:line) | Fixture replacement |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `OFFLINE_DEBUG_LOG_DIR` | `pim-offline-client/src/config/settings.rs:326` | `Settings::log_dir_for_tests(&Path)` |
| `OFFLINE_DEBUG_CONFIG_DIR` | `pim-offline-client/src/config/settings.rs:401` | `Settings::save_to_file_at(&Path)` / `Settings::load_from_dir(&Path)` |
| `OFFLINE_DEBUG_RUNTIME_STATUS_DIR` | `pim-offline-client/src/runtime_status.rs:197` | `RuntimeStatus::write_to_dir(&Path)` |
| `PIM_OFFLINE_IPC_ELEVATION_PATH` | `pim-offline-client/src/ipc/paths.rs:38, 45` | `IpcServer::bind_at(&str)` + `IpcClient::connect_at(&str)` |
| `OFFLINE_DEV_FIXTURES` | `pim-offline-server/src/bin/seed_dev/main.rs:106` | seed-dev is a binary; tests must not import it |
| `OFFLINE_ADMIN_TOKEN` | `pim-offline-server/src/auth/admin.rs` | `AdminAuth::with_token(&str)` |
| `ENABLE_LEGACY_COMPAT` | `pim-offline-server/src/api/legacy/…` | `LegacyTranslator::enabled(bool)` |
| `LOCALE_ENV_VAR` constant | `pim-app-config/crates/pim-app-config-i18n/src/locale.rs` | `Locale::override_for_tests(&str)` |

Any new env-var read that doesn't appear in this table must arrive
with the matching fixture API in the same change set, and the table
above must be updated.

## Test fixtures that already exist (use these, don't invent new ones)

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Throwaway program id for keyring / HKLM tests | `pim_offline_client::secret_storage::elevated_local_storage_tests::test_program_id()` produces a unique `pim-e2e-<uuid>` per test |
| Sandboxed config + log dir | `tempfile::TempDir::new()?` + the explicit-path variant on the type under test |
| In-memory `pim-config-storage` backend | `pim_config_storage::InMemoryBackend::new()` under `cfg(test)` |
| Sandboxed pipe / socket name | `let pipe = format!("{}aic-test-{}-elev", PIPE_PREFIX, uuid::Uuid::new_v4())` then pass to `IpcServer::bind_at` / `IpcClient::connect_at` |
| Mock SCM status sink | `pim_shutdown::scm::MockStatusSink` (see `pim-shutdown/docs/INTEGRATION.md`) |

## Forbidden constructs

In every file under `tests/`, `**/*_tests.rs`, `**/tests.rs`,
`**/integration_tests.rs`, `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { … }` blocks,
and any `examples/` that asserts behavior:

- `std::env::set_var(…)` / `env::set_var(…)` — banned outright.
- `std::env::remove_var(…)` — same reason.
- `std::fs::create_dir_all("/etc/aic/…")` / `…
 "C:\\ProgramData\\AIC\\…")` — banned outright.
- `winreg::enums::HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE` opens — banned in tests;
 use HKCU under a `test-<uuid>` subkey or the in-memory backend.
- `keyring::Entry::new("pim-offline-agent", …)` / any production
 service-name string — banned in tests; use
 `test_program_id()`.
- Hard-coded pipe paths (`r"\\.\pipe\aic-offline-agent-service\elevation"`
 etc.) — banned in tests; bind a unique per-test pipe name.
- `tokio::net::TcpListener::bind("0.0.0.0:8443")` / any
 deterministic port — use `bind("127.0.0.1:0")` and read the
 actual port back via `local_addr()`.

## Required production-code pattern

Every type that reads a path / channel / handle from a machine-global
store today must expose two surfaces:

```rust
impl Settings {
    /// Production path: resolves OFFLINE_DEBUG_CONFIG_DIR if set,
    /// else the platform default under %PROGRAMDATA% / /etc.
    pub fn save_to_default_location(&self) -> Result<()> {
        let dir = Self::default_config_dir()?;
        self.save_to_file_at(&dir.join("settings.json"))
    }

    /// Fixture path: explicit, no env-var read, no platform lookup.
    /// Tests call this with a `TempDir` they own.
    pub fn save_to_file_at(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<()> {
        let bytes = serde_json::to_vec_pretty(self)
            .context("serialize Settings")?;
        std::fs::write(path, bytes)
            .with_context(|| format!("write {}", path.display()))?;
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

Tests then look like:

```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn settings_round_trip() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let dir = tempfile::TempDir::new()?;
    let path = dir.path().join("settings.json");
    let s = Settings::default();
    s.save_to_file_at(&path)?;
    let loaded = Settings::load_from_file_at(&path)?;
    assert_eq!(s, loaded);
    Ok(())
}
```

No `set_var`. No write outside the `TempDir`. The test cleans up on
drop. Parallel runs do not race.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (today, `pim-offline-client/tests/integration_tests.rs:125`):

```rust
let temp_dir = tempfile::TempDir::new()?;
std::env::set_var("OFFLINE_DEBUG_CONFIG_DIR", temp_dir.path());
let settings = Settings::load_from_default_location()?;
```

**Fix** (after the fixture-API change lands in
`pim-offline-client/src/config/settings.rs`):

```rust
let temp_dir = tempfile::TempDir::new()?;
let settings = Settings::load_from_dir(temp_dir.path())?;
```

The env-var production path stays intact for operators who set
`OFFLINE_DEBUG_CONFIG_DIR` for debugging; tests stop racing on it.

## Where this is currently enforced

| Repo | Status |
| --- | --- |
| `pim-offline-client` (`Settings`, `RuntimeStatus`, IPC paths) | partial — fixture APIs in flight under Wave 1 Track C |
| `pim-offline-server` (`AdminAuth`, legacy compat, seed-dev) | partial — `AdminAuth::with_token` exists; `ENABLE_LEGACY_COMPAT` tests still mutate env |
| `pim-app-config` / `pim-app-config-i18n` | audit ongoing — `Locale::override_for_tests` planned |
| `pim-config-storage` | compliant — in-memory backend exists; tests must select it explicitly |
| Sibling configurator / elevation crates | inherit fixture APIs from the libraries above |

The "audit ongoing" / "partial" rows are not necessarily defective;
they are unverified. A future PR that grows a new `env::set_var` in
a test body is rejected at review.

